# ── Jalebi environment variables (documentation only) ────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.  `.env` is git-ignored —
# NEVER commit a real token anywhere in this repo.  See AGENTS.md → Security rules.

# Required: fine-grained GitHub personal access token (owner's own account).
# DANGER: treat as a secret.  Do not commit, do not log, do not paste into prompts.
# Scopes required by Jalebi (PRD §F1):
#   classic:  repo
#   fine-grained: Contents (read/write), Pull requests (read/write),
#                 Issues (read/write), Metadata (read), Commit statuses (read/write)
# Every PAT is an equal NAMED ACCOUNT: add accounts via the GitHub page UI
# (stored in <data-dir>/secrets.json, 0600). There is NO primary/default token
# and NO fallback — the account selected for a task is the one used.
# JALEBI_GITHUB_TOKEN below is used ONLY for masking (so a stray value never
# survives into logs); it never resolves which account runs anything.
# NEVER use the `gh` CLI.  NEVER use any other token/credential.
JALEBI_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Required: UI password (PRD §F13). The server binds to 0.0.0.0 for LAN access
# by default and refuses to start when this is empty.
# When set, every route except /api/health requires HTTP Basic auth (browser prompt).
JALEBI_PASSWORD=

# Optional: public URLs for notification tap-links (LAN, Tailscale, tunnel…).
# Comma-separated `Label=url` list; the first is the default tap target and each
# URL gets its own "Open (<label>)" button (max 3 buttons). Unset → 127.0.0.1 links.
# JALEBI_PUBLIC_URLS=LAN=http://192.0.2.1:2052, Tailscale=http://198.51.100.5:2052

# Optional: data directory (defaults to ~/.jalebi)
# JALEBI_DATA_DIR=

# Optional: host/port the orchestrator binds to (binds to 0.0.0.0 for LAN access by default)
# JALEBI_HOST=0.0.0.0
# JALEBI_PORT=2052